;;
;; creeperdiamonds.xyz — apex records for the Cloud Run domain mapping
;;
;; Import in Cloudflare: DNS > Records > Import and Export > Import DNS records.
;;
;; THIS FILE ADDS. IT DOES NOT REMOVE.
;; Cloudflare's importer merges records in; it never deletes what is already
;; there. The apex is currently on registrar parking with six A records, and
;; importing without deleting them first leaves TEN A records at the apex.
;; A visitor then reaches the parking host or Cloud Run depending on which
;; record their resolver happens to pick, which is worse than the broken
;; state it replaced because it fails for only some people.
;;
;; DELETE THESE FIRST (type A, name creeperdiamonds.xyz):
;;   82.22.5.17   82.22.5.20   82.22.5.22
;;   82.22.5.24   82.22.5.25   104.167.24.195
;;
;; DO NOT DELETE ANYTHING ELSE. In particular the zone already holds:
;;   MX  route1/route2/route3.mx.cloudflare.net  — Cloudflare Email Routing,
;;       which is what makes contact@creeperdiamonds.xyz deliverable. The
;;       site publishes that address, and a published address that bounces
;;       is worse than none because the sender believes they reached someone.
;;   TXT records — SPF and the Email Routing verification live here.
;;   CNAME appealy -> ghs.googlehosted.com — the working Appealy mapping.
;; None of them are in this file, so importing cannot touch them. Deleting
;; them by hand while clearing the parking records would break mail.
;;
;; SET PROXY STATUS TO "DNS ONLY" (grey cloud) ON IMPORT.
;; Cloud Run issues and renews its own certificate by reaching these records.
;; A proxied record puts Cloudflare's certificate in front of that process and
;; the mapping never validates — CertificateProvisioned stays Unknown forever
;; with no error that says why.
;;
;; Values issued by:
;;   gcloud beta run domain-mappings create --service=appealy \
;;     --domain=creeperdiamonds.xyz --region=us-central1 \
;;     --project=yahav-project-505809
;;
;; Re-run that command rather than trusting this file if the mapping is ever
;; recreated. These are Google's standard anycast addresses and have been
;; stable for years, but a checked-in file is not the system of record.
;;
;; TTL 1 is Cloudflare's "Auto".
;;

;; A records — IPv4
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	A	216.239.32.21
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	A	216.239.34.21
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	A	216.239.36.21
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	A	216.239.38.21

;; AAAA records — IPv6
;; Not optional. Google's mapping expects both families, and a v6-only client
;; that gets no AAAA falls back inconsistently rather than cleanly.
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	AAAA	2001:4860:4802:32::15
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	AAAA	2001:4860:4802:34::15
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	AAAA	2001:4860:4802:36::15
creeperdiamonds.xyz.	1	IN	AAAA	2001:4860:4802:38::15
